Chapter: ProbeClosureSaturated

 A SATURATED call whose result type is a function. No recursion anywhere,
 no self call, nothing that could be compiled as a loop.

 `make-adder` takes one argument and returns a function. `relay-once`
 calls it with exactly one argument, so the call is saturated and should
 simply return what make-adder returns.

 `relayed-once 47` means saturated calls returning a function are fine and
 the wrong answer seen in the mutual-recursion probe needs another
 explanation. Anything else -- particularly a number in the bivy heap
 range around 6291456 -- means a saturated call returning a function is
 not being called at all, and this is a silent miscompilation reachable
 without any recursion.

Section: Shapes

  add3 : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  add3 (x) (y) (z) = x + y + z

  make-adder : Integer -> (Integer, Integer -> Integer)
  make-adder (n) = add3 n

 One saturated call. Nothing else.

  relay-once : Integer -> (Integer, Integer -> Integer)
  relay-once (n) = make-adder n

Section: Driver

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("direct 47 expected: " & show (((make-adder 5) 20) 22))
    print-line-uni ("relayed-once 47 expected: " & show (((relay-once 5) 20) 22))
  end
